Package: opencode
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: Development
Priority: optional
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
Recommends: git
Homepage: https://github.com/Justintunsday/opencode-ios
Description: OpenCode v2 CLI for jailbroken iOS (rootless, /var/jb)
 OpenCode is an open-source AI coding agent for the terminal. This package
 ships the upstream OpenCode v2 CLI through its official Node.js build path
 running on a native iPhoneOS arm64 Node.js 22.9.0 runtime. Everything is
 installed rootless beneath /var/jb, so it does not modify the iOS system
 partition.
 .
 Target device for this build: iPhone SE (2nd generation), arm64, iOS 16.1.1
 with the Dopamine rootless jailbreak; the launcher is /var/jb/usr/bin/opencode.
 .
 Features that depend on native addons without iPhoneOS builds (interactive
 PTY terminal panes, native file watchers, ffi/fff) are disabled or degrade
 to documented fallbacks. See the packaged KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md.
 .
 Device execution is UNVERIFIED ON DEVICE by CI. Run the packaged
 device-smoke.sh and see /var/jb/usr/share/doc/opencode/VERIFICATION.md.
